    "https://www.trinitycollege.edu/associate-professor-of-business-organizational-leadership/": {
      "title": "Associate Professor of Business Organizational Leadership",
      "description": "Associate Professor of Business Organizational Leadership - Trinity College Skip to main content Oasis V4 Oasis V5 Canvas Login Academic Calendar Resources Request Information Apply Now Hit enter to search or ESC to close Search Close Search search Menu Academics & Degrees Academic Catalog Bachelor of Arts (Day) Associate of Arts (Day) Bachelor of Science (Evenings) Certificate Programs Dual Enrollment Honors Program Admissions & Tuition Admissions Presidential Scholarship Financial Aid Tuition Military/Veterans New Student Checklist About TCF About Trinity Accreditation Student’s Right to Know Alumni Faculty Faculty Publications Student Life Academic Calendar Canvas Login Oasis V4 Oasis V5 Library Resources Student Life Interactive 360° Experience Athletics Athletics Staff Directory TCF Athletics Men’s Baseball Men’s Basketball Men’s Football Men’s Soccer Women’s Basketball Women’s Softball Women’s Volleyball Tiger Booster Club Giving Church Matching Grant Forge a Future General Giving Giving Tuesday Life Change Scholarship Scholarship Chapel W.T. Watson Society search Business Organizational Leadership Department Associate Professor of Business Organizational Leadership Position Overview Title Department Chair & Associate Professor of Business Organizational Leadership Department Business Organizational Leadership Department Reports to Vice President for Academic Affairs Location Trinity College of Florida (Trinity, FL — On-site) Contract Period July 1 – June 30 (Annual Contract) Compensation Competitive salary commensurate with experience/rank (includes medical insurance, term life insurance policy, and 401(k) retirement plan; moving expense reimbursement assistance available) Position Summary Trinity College of Florida seeks an experienced, biblically grounded academic leader to serve as Department Chair and Faculty Member in the Business Organizational Leadership Department. This role combines full-time classroom teaching, curriculum design, program assessment, faculty development, and departmental leadership. The Chair serves as the primary steward of the Business Organizational Leadership curriculum, ensuring academic excellence, strategic workforce relevance, and integration of a Christian worldview across all organizational leadership courses. Key Responsibilities 1. Departmental Administration & Leadership Curriculum Design & Innovation: Initiate and oversee course and curricular design, continuous program reviews, and enhancements within the Business Organizational Leadership Department to align with academic and marketplace standards. Assessment & Planning: Conduct annual assessment and strategic planning for departmental improvement; compile and present findings and action plans to the Assessment and Planning Committee. Teach-Out & Articulation Assistance: Assist in developing teach-out plans and articulation agreements for incoming transfer students from closing or partnering institutions. Budget & Operations: Oversee departmental budgeting, planning, and academic policy reviews in alignment with institutional priorities. 2. Teaching & Academic Advising Instructional Load: Teach 12 to 18 credit hours per semester across traditional day, in-seat, and/or online formats within the Business Organizational Leadership discipline. Academic Advising & Consulting: Provide academic consulting and course planning to the Director of Student Success and deliver direct academic advising and mentoring to students majoring in Business Organizational Leadership. Academic Freedom: Exercise academic freedom in accordance with the college’s Faculty Handbook and Statement of Faith. 3. Faculty Recruitment, Vetting & Evaluation Faculty Search & Hiring: Collaborate with the Vice President for Academic Affairs and the President in identifying personnel needs, vetting credentials, and interviewing candidates for full-time and adjunct faculty appointments within the department. Adjunct Faculty Supervision & Evaluation: Conduct annual evaluations of adjunct business instructors with 5 years or less of teaching experience, and biannual evaluations of adjunct instructors with over 5 years of teaching experience. Classroom Observations: Participate in candidate campus interviews, evaluating sample teaching sessions and professional experience in management and organizational leadership. 4. Campus Engagement, Committees & Spiritual Mentorship Governance: Actively serve on appointed faculty and institutional committees governing the academic and administrative affairs of the college. Student Discipleship: Actively develop discipleship relationships with students and facilitate/lead a weekly student small group or ministry cohort. College Representation: Articulate and represent the vision of Trinity College of Florida positively to students, staff, alumni, local churches, and professional/business networks. Qualifications & Requirements Required Education & Academic Credentials Terminal Degree Preferred: An earned academic doctorate (Ph.D., D.B.A., Ed.D., or related terminal degree) in Business Administration, Organizational Leadership, Management, or a closely related field from a regionally accredited graduate institution is strongly preferred. Minimum Requirement: A master’s degree (e.g., MBA, M.A., or M.S.) from a regionally accredited institution with a minimum of 18 graduate semester credit hours completed directly within the business/leadership teaching discipline. Candidates nearing completion of their terminal degree (ABD) may be considered. Experience & Skills Demonstrated excellence or strong potential for excellence in undergraduate and/or graduate business education. Practical executive, entrepreneurial, or management leadership experience in the business or nonprofit sector. Proven background in curriculum evaluation, academic assessment, departmental budgeting, and strategic planning. Strong interpersonal, written communication, and public speaking skills, with the capacity to work collegially across diverse campus constituencies. Faith & Lifestyle Standards Profess and model a vibrant personal faith in Jesus Christ, upholding the Biblical standard of personal conduct and Christian lifestyle. Full unreserved agreement with and adherence to the Trinity College of Florida Statement of Faith, Mission, Vision, Values, and Lifestyle statement, and the Faculty Handbook. Application Instructions Interested candidates must submit their application materials directly to Jackie Burden: Completed Faculty Application Form Comprehensive Curriculum Vitae (CV) / Resume Personal Christian Testimony and Statement of Faith Copies of all official graduate and undergraduate transcripts Three professional letters of reference speaking to teaching ability, leadership experience, and Christian character Please direct resumes, applications, and related inquiries to: Jackie Burden jackie.burden@trinitycollege.edu Request Information Apply Now Admissions@Trinitycollege.Edu 800.388.0869 2430 Welbilt Blvd. Trinity, FL 34655 Academic Catalog Accreditation ABHE Administration Directory Campus Security and Facilities Maintenance Church Matching Grant College Calendar Donate Ensuring a Respectful Campus Refer a Friend Pastor/Alumni Referral Grant Form Student Counseling Services Title IX Annual Security Report Gainful Employment Grievances Office of Institutional Effectiveness Privacy Rights Resources Careers Accessibility © 2026 Trinity College. All Rights Reserved. twitter facebook linkedin youtube instagram Close Menu Academics & Degrees Academic Catalog Bachelor of Arts (Day) Associate of Arts (Day) Bachelor of Science (Evenings) Certificate Programs Dual Enrollment Honors Program Admissions & Tuition Admissions Presidential Scholarship Financial Aid Tuition Military/Veterans New Student Checklist About TCF About Trinity Accreditation Student’s Right to Know Alumni Faculty Faculty Publications Student Life Academic Calendar Canvas Login Oasis V4 Oasis V5 Library Resources Student Life Interactive 360° Experience Athletics Athletics Staff Directory TCF Athletics Men’s Baseball Men’s Basketball Men’s Football Men’s Soccer Women’s Basketball Women’s Softball Women’s Volleyball Tiger Booster Club Giving Church Matching Grant Forge a Future General Giving Giving Tuesday Life Change Scholarship Scholarship Chapel W.T. Watson Society Oasis V4 Oasis V5 Canvas Login Academic Calendar Resources Request Information Apply Now"
    },
    "https://www.trinitycollege.edu/assistant-professor-of-general-studies/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of General Studies",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of General Studies - Trinity College Skip to main content Oasis V4 Oasis V5 Canvas Login Academic Calendar Resources Request Information Apply Now Hit enter to search or ESC to close Search Close Search search Menu Academics & Degrees Academic Catalog Bachelor of Arts (Day) Associate of Arts (Day) Bachelor of Science (Evenings) Certificate Programs Dual Enrollment Honors Program Admissions & Tuition Admissions Presidential Scholarship Financial Aid Tuition Military/Veterans New Student Checklist About TCF About Trinity Accreditation Student’s Right to Know Alumni Faculty Faculty Publications Student Life Academic Calendar Canvas Login Oasis V4 Oasis V5 Library Resources Student Life Interactive 360° Experience Athletics Athletics Staff Directory TCF Athletics Men’s Baseball Men’s Basketball Men’s Football Men’s Soccer Women’s Basketball Women’s Softball Women’s Volleyball Tiger Booster Club Giving Church Matching Grant Forge a Future General Giving Giving Tuesday Life Change Scholarship Scholarship Chapel W.T. Watson Society search Assistant Professor of General Studies Position Summary This is a full-time faculty position within the General Studies Department in the Traditional Day Program. Salary and Benefits ● Salary: Commensurate with Experience ● Benefits: Medical insurance, $15,000 term life policy, and 401K retirement program ● Moving expenses reimbursed up to $3500 Reports to: President Location: Trinity College of Florida – Trinity, Florida Remote: No Primary Responsibilities Teach a minimum of 12 credit hours per semester (maximum of 18 credits), including both in-seat and online courses. Serve as Program Chair of the General Department, providing leadership, advising, and oversight for the department. Serve on college committees as outlined in the Faculty Handbook. Contract begins July 1, 2026 Develop discipleship relationships with students and lead a weekly small group. Uphold and promote academic freedom in alignment with the college’s Statement of Faith and faculty policies. General Requirements Master’s degree from an accredited institution, with a minimum of 18 credit hours in english. Submit the following materials to Christopher Gates, PhD, President, and Krista Mallo, PhD, Executive Advisor for Academics: ○ Curriculum Vitae ○ Three letters of reference ○ Statement of faith and personal testimony ○ Official transcripts ○ Completed Faculty Application Form Send to christopher.gates@trinitycollege.edu , & krista.mallo.faculty@trinitycollege.edu Minimum of five years of teaching experience in a classroom. Demonstrated potential for excellence in college-level instruction. Record of promising scholarly achievement. Ability to work collaboratively and professionally with students, faculty, and staff. Experience with budgeting, planning, and policy review. Strong interpersonal, written, and public speaking skills, with the ability to represent the college to diverse populations. Ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a team. Conditions of Employment Model the Biblical standard of personal conduct and lifestyle. Support and adhere to the Mission, Vision, Values, and Lifestyle Statement of Trinity College of Florida. Affirm and support the Statement of Faith of Trinity College of Florida. Comply with all policies outlined in the Faculty Handbook and Policies and Procedures Handbook. Contract Period: July 1 – June 30 annually and renewable each year. Request Information Apply Now Admissions@Trinitycollege.Edu 800.388.0869 2430 Welbilt Blvd. Trinity, FL 34655 Academic Catalog Accreditation ABHE Administration Directory Campus Security and Facilities Maintenance Church Matching Grant College Calendar Donate Ensuring a Respectful Campus Refer a Friend Pastor/Alumni Referral Grant Form Student Counseling Services Title IX Annual Security Report Gainful Employment Grievances Office of Institutional Effectiveness Privacy Rights Resources Careers Accessibility © 2026 Trinity College. All Rights Reserved. twitter facebook linkedin youtube instagram Close Menu Academics & Degrees Academic Catalog Bachelor of Arts (Day) Associate of Arts (Day) Bachelor of Science (Evenings) Certificate Programs Dual Enrollment Honors Program Admissions & Tuition Admissions Presidential Scholarship Financial Aid Tuition Military/Veterans New Student Checklist About TCF About Trinity Accreditation Student’s Right to Know Alumni Faculty Faculty Publications Student Life Academic Calendar Canvas Login Oasis V4 Oasis V5 Library Resources Student Life Interactive 360° Experience Athletics Athletics Staff Directory TCF Athletics Men’s Baseball Men’s Basketball Men’s Football Men’s Soccer Women’s Basketball Women’s Softball Women’s Volleyball Tiger Booster Club Giving Church Matching Grant Forge a Future General Giving Giving Tuesday Life Change Scholarship Scholarship Chapel W.T. Watson Society Oasis V4 Oasis V5 Canvas Login Academic Calendar Resources Request Information Apply Now"
    },
    "https://www.trinitycollege.edu/general-studies-adjunct-pool/": {
      "title": "General Studies Adjunct Pool",
      "description": "General Studies Adjunct Pool - Trinity College Skip to main content Oasis V4 Oasis V5 Canvas Login Academic Calendar Resources Request Information Apply Now Hit enter to search or ESC to close Search Close Search search Menu Academics & Degrees Academic Catalog Bachelor of Arts (Day) Associate of Arts (Day) Bachelor of Science (Evenings) Certificate Programs Dual Enrollment Honors Program Admissions & Tuition Admissions Presidential Scholarship Financial Aid Tuition Military/Veterans New Student Checklist About TCF About Trinity Accreditation Student’s Right to Know Alumni Faculty Faculty Publications Student Life Academic Calendar Canvas Login Oasis V4 Oasis V5 Library Resources Student Life Interactive 360° Experience Athletics Athletics Staff Directory TCF Athletics Men’s Baseball Men’s Basketball Men’s Football Men’s Soccer Women’s Basketball Women’s Softball Women’s Volleyball Tiger Booster Club Giving Church Matching Grant Forge a Future General Giving Giving Tuesday Life Change Scholarship Scholarship Chapel W.T. Watson Society search General Studies Adjunct Faculty The General Studies Department of Trinity College of Florida is seeking qualified candidates for its adjunct faculty pool in the areas of English, Mathematics, Science, History, Economics, Geography, Communications, Music, Piano, and Fine Arts. The department is seeking adjunct faculty who will be available for teaching both face-to-face and online classes. A master’s degree with 18 graduate credits in the teaching discipline is required for consideration. Experience with student-centered instruction and hybrid modalities is highly desired. Qualified candidates who are in agreement with the doctrinal statement of the College (see doctrinal statement) may send their letter of interest and CV to Dr. Krista Mallo at krista.mallo.faculty@trinitycollege. edu . Request Information Apply Now Admissions@Trinitycollege.Edu 800.388.0869 2430 Welbilt Blvd. Trinity, FL 34655 Academic Catalog Accreditation ABHE Administration Directory Campus Security and Facilities Maintenance Church Matching Grant College Calendar Donate Ensuring a Respectful Campus Refer a Friend Pastor/Alumni Referral Grant Form Student Counseling Services Title IX Annual Security Report Gainful Employment Grievances Office of Institutional Effectiveness Privacy Rights Resources Careers Accessibility © 2026 Trinity College. All Rights Reserved. twitter facebook linkedin youtube instagram Close Menu Academics & Degrees Back Academic Catalog Bachelor of Arts (Day) Associate of Arts (Day) Bachelor of Science (Evenings) Certificate Programs Dual Enrollment Honors Program Admissions & Tuition Back Admissions Presidential Scholarship Financial Aid Tuition Military/Veterans New Student Checklist About TCF Back About Trinity Accreditation Student’s Right to Know Alumni Faculty Faculty Publications Student Life Back Academic Calendar Canvas Login Oasis V4 Oasis V5 Library Resources Student Life Interactive 360° Experience Athletics Back Athletics Staff Directory TCF Athletics Men’s Baseball Men’s Basketball Men’s Football Men’s Soccer Women’s Basketball Women’s Softball Women’s Volleyball Tiger Booster Club Giving Back Church Matching Grant Forge a Future General Giving Giving Tuesday Life Change Scholarship Scholarship Chapel W.T. Watson Society Oasis V4 Oasis V5 Canvas Login Academic Calendar Resources Request Information Apply Now"
    },
    "https://www.trinitycollege.edu/general-studies-department-chair-english-professor/": {
      "title": "General Studies Department Chair/ English Professor (Open Rank)",
      "description": "General Studies Department Chair/English Professor - Trinity College Skip to main content Oasis V4 Oasis V5 Canvas Login Academic Calendar Resources Request Information Apply Now Hit enter to search or ESC to close Search Close Search search Menu Academics & Degrees Academic Catalog Bachelor of Arts (Day) Associate of Arts (Day) Bachelor of Science (Evenings) Certificate Programs Dual Enrollment Honors Program Admissions & Tuition Admissions Presidential Scholarship Financial Aid Tuition Military/Veterans New Student Checklist About TCF About Trinity Accreditation Student’s Right to Know Alumni Faculty Faculty Publications Student Life Academic Calendar Canvas Login Oasis V4 Oasis V5 Library Resources Student Life Interactive 360° Experience Athletics Athletics Staff Directory TCF Athletics Men’s Baseball Men’s Basketball Men’s Football Men’s Soccer Women’s Basketball Women’s Softball Women’s Volleyball Tiger Booster Club Giving Church Matching Grant Forge a Future General Giving Giving Tuesday Life Change Scholarship Scholarship Chapel W.T. Watson Society search General Studies Department Chair/ English Professor (Open Rank) Reposted: previous applicants will be considered. Overview Title Department Chair of General Studies & English Professor (Open Rank) Department General Studies Department Reports to Vice President for Academic Affairs Location Trinity College of Florida (Trinity, FL — On-site) Expected Start Date July 1, 2027 Contract Period July 1 – June 30 (Annual Contract) Compensation Competitive salary commensurate with experience/rank (includes medical insurance, $15,000 term life insurance policy, and 401(k) retirement plan; moving expense reimbursement up to $3,500) Position Summary Trinity College of Florida seeks an experienced, biblically grounded academic leader to serve as Department Chair of General Studies and full-time English faculty member in the Traditional Day Program. This role combines full-time classroom teaching in English, including Composition, Literature, and Advanced Research Writing, with curriculum design, program assessment, faculty development, and departmental leadership. The Chair serves as the primary steward of the General Studies curriculum, ensuring academic excellence, strong foundational skills in writing and critical thinking, and integration of a Christian worldview across all General Studies courses. Key Responsibilities 1. Departmental Administration & Leadership Department Chair: Serve as Chair of the General Studies Department, providing leadership, advising, and oversight for the department. Curriculum Design & Innovation: Initiate and oversee course and curricular design, continuous program reviews, and enhancements within the General Studies Department to align with academic and accreditation standards. Assessment & Planning: Conduct annual assessment and strategic planning for departmental improvement; compile and present findings and action plans to the Assessment and Planning Committee. Budgeting & Policy: Participate in departmental budgeting, planning, and policy review. 2. Teaching & Academic Advising Instructional Load: Teach a minimum of 12 to 15 credit hours per semester across in-seat and online formats, including English Composition, Literature, and Advanced Research Writing. Academic Advising: Provide academic advising to students, in collaboration with other College departments, such as Student Development. Academic Freedom: Exercise academic freedom in accordance with the College’s Faculty Handbook and Statement of Faith. 3. Faculty Recruitment, Vetting & Evaluation Faculty Search & Hiring: Collaborate with the Vice President for Academic Affairs and the President in identifying personnel needs, vetting credentials, and interviewing candidates for full-time and adjunct faculty appointments within the department. Adjunct Faculty Supervision & Evaluation: Conduct annual evaluations of adjunct professors within the department in accordance with the College’s current policies. Classroom Observations: Participate in candidate campus interviews, evaluating sample teaching sessions and relevant instructional experience. 4. Campus Service, Committees & Spiritual Mentorship Service: Actively serve on appointed faculty and institutional committees as outlined in the Faculty Handbook. Student Discipleship: Actively develop discipleship relationships with students and facilitate/lead a weekly student small group. College Representation: Articulate and represent the vision of Trinity College of Florida positively to students, staff, alumni, local churches, and the broader community. Qualifications & Requirements Required Education & Academic Credentials Minimum Requirement: A conferred master’s degree from a regionally accredited institution with a minimum of 18 graduate semester credit hours in English, Rhetoric, Composition, or Literature. Terminal Degree Preferred: An earned academic doctorate or related terminal degree in English, Rhetoric, Composition, Literature, or a closely related field from a regionally accredited institution is preferred. Experience & Skills Minimum of five years of classroom teaching experience. Demonstrated excellence or strong potential for excellence in college-level instruction in composition and literature. Record of promising scholarly achievement. Experience with curriculum evaluation, academic assessment, departmental budgeting, planning, and policy review. Strong interpersonal, written communication, and public speaking skills, with the capacity to work collegially, both independently and as part of a team, across diverse campus constituencies. Faith & Lifestyle Standards Profess and model a vibrant personal faith in Jesus Christ, upholding the Biblical standard of personal conduct and Christian lifestyle. Full unreserved agreement with and adherence to the Trinity College of Florida Statement of Faith, Mission, Vision, Values, and Lifestyle Statement, and the Faculty Handbook and Policies and Procedures Handbook. Application Instructions This position has been reposted; previous applicants will be considered. Interested candidates must submit their application materials directly to Christopher Gates, PhD, President, and Krista Mallo, PhD, Executive Advisor for Academics: Completed Faculty Application Form Comprehensive Curriculum Vitae (CV) / Resume Personal Christian Testimony and Statement of Faith Copies of all official graduate and undergraduate transcripts Three professional letters of reference speaking to teaching ability, leadership experience, and Christian character Please direct resumes, applications, and related inquiries to: Christopher Gates, PhD, President — christopher.gates@trinitycollege.edu Krista Mallo, PhD, Executive Advisor for Academics — krista.mallo.faculty@trinitycollege.edu Request Information Apply Now Admissions@Trinitycollege.Edu 800.388.0869 2430 Welbilt Blvd. Trinity, FL 34655 Academic Catalog Accreditation ABHE Administration Directory Campus Security and Facilities Maintenance Church Matching Grant College Calendar Donate Ensuring a Respectful Campus Refer a Friend Pastor/Alumni Referral Grant Form Student Counseling Services Title IX TCF’s Commitment to Excellence, Responsibility, Trust Annual Security Report Gainful Employment Grievances Office of Institutional Effectiveness Privacy Rights Resources Careers Accessibility © 2026 Trinity College. All Rights Reserved. twitter facebook linkedin youtube instagram Close Menu Academics & Degrees Academic Catalog Bachelor of Arts (Day) Associate of Arts (Day) Bachelor of Science (Evenings) Certificate Programs Dual Enrollment Honors Program Admissions & Tuition Admissions Presidential Scholarship Financial Aid Tuition Military/Veterans New Student Checklist About TCF About Trinity Accreditation Student’s Right to Know Alumni Faculty Faculty Publications Student Life Academic Calendar Canvas Login Oasis V4 Oasis V5 Library Resources Student Life Interactive 360° Experience Athletics Athletics Staff Directory TCF Athletics Men’s Baseball Men’s Basketball Men’s Football Men’s Soccer Women’s Basketball Women’s Softball Women’s Volleyball Tiger Booster Club Giving Church Matching Grant Forge a Future General Giving Giving Tuesday Life Change Scholarship Scholarship Chapel W.T. Watson Society Oasis V4 Oasis V5 Canvas Login Academic Calendar Resources Request Information Apply Now"
    }
